49-55.\n\nThe first nine files retain their prior 34-block inventory; test_terraform_corroborator.py contributes four independently validated comment regions, producing 38 blocks across 10 paths.\n\n## Preservation boundaries\nPreserve backend/failure coverage, closed abstention reasons, worker isolation/reaping, detector quarantine and attribution, validation deduplication/fan-out, confirm-only dependency/environment resolution, import-clean non-adoption, polyglot collision/member/workspace/alias/stdlib guards, deterministic extraction, yield floors, and zero false refutes.\n\nFor test_terraform_corroborator.py preserve positive-only corroboration, read-only snapshot isolation, relative position/path safety, redaction, retry/cleanup, and closed abstention. Keep its concise module docstring at line 1; mechanism marker at line 23; generated runtime-string shebang at 104 and comment payload at 131-136; concise baseline comment at 322; and every other unlisted comment unchanged. The generated script text is runtime content.\n\nPreserve all runtime strings and every physical directive line. At the basis those are the mechanism-ok/noqa line in test_terraform_corroborator.py and three type: ignore[arg-type] lines in test_harness.py. The '# noqa: BLE0001' text inside the editable test_worker_entry_propagates_interrupts docstring is prose, not a source directive. Also preserve the concise import/distribution guard at test_polyglot_corpus.py:223-224 and yield calibration at test_yield_eval.py:42-44.\n\n## Implementation and review\nCapture immutable before/final blobs. For Python, parse with ast.parse(source, type_comments=True), replace only the allowlisted leading owner docstrings, normalize only ast.TypeIgnore.lineno, and require exact ast.dump(..., include_attributes=False) equality. The zero-context hunk oracle permits changes only inside the listed base spans; the directive/shebang oracle compares protected physical lines. Do not change adjacent blank lines.\n\nA non-author reviewer posts exactly 38 leaf-linked TSV rows:\nstable_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>final_words<TAB>semantic_preservation<TAB>bloat_removal<TAB>reviewer_session\nCitations use full SHAs; every final word count is smaller and all three verdicts are PASS.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Prose changes occur only inside the 38 allowlisted blocks.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts exactly 38 leaf-linked TSV rows, one for each allowlisted block.\n- [ ] Every reviewer row uses this schema: stable_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>final_words<TAB>semantic_preservation<TAB>bloat_removal<TAB>reviewer_session.\n- [ ] Every before_citation uses the full immutable SHA d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84.\n- [ ] Every final_citation uses the full final commit SHA.\n- [ ] Every row records final_words < before_words.\n- [ ] Every row records directives_exact=PASS.\n- [ ] Every row records semantic_preservation=PASS, confirming its preserved_contract_or_consumer.\n- [ ] Every row records bloat_removal=PASS, confirming removal of chronology, repetition, narration, or separator ornament.\n- [ ] The immutable-base AST/runtime oracle passes for all 10 owned paths.\n- [ ] The protected-line oracle passes for all 10 owned paths.\n- [ ] The base-span oracle passes for all 10 owned paths.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the 10 file-impact paths.\n- [ ] All seven structured verify commands pass.\n- [ ] Every concrete command listed under Verification exits 0.\n## Verification\nThe persisted immutable-prose-only command contains the exact owner/span map and is authoritative for semantic and comment boundaries. Run it, then run this literal zsh session from the leaf worktree:\n\n~~~zsh\nR=tests/unit/grounding\npaths=(\n$R/test_conformance.py\n$R/test_coverage_reconstruction.py\n$R/test_engine_b.py\n$R/test_environment_resolution.py\n$R/test_harness.py\n$R/test_non_adoption.py\n$R/test_polyglot_corpus.py\n$R/test_resolve.py\n$R/test_terraform_corroborator.py\n$R/test_yield_eval.py\n)\nrtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import subprocess,sys\nexpected=sorted(sys.argv[1:]); actual=sorted(subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--name-only\",\"HEAD^..HEAD\"],text=True).splitlines())\nif actual!=expected: raise SystemExit((actual,expected))' \"${paths[@]}\"\nrtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest -q \"${paths[@]}\"\nrtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" ruff check \"${paths[@]}\"\nrtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" ruff format --check \"${paths[@]}\"\nrtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py\nrtk git diff --check HEAD^..HEAD -- \"${paths[@]}\"\nrtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify\n~~~\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788664072598281001,"uuid":"d1df9a86-f075-4b61-977f-0ef57540b61a"}